{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Follow-up task likable-waterworn-willet (ab45-2cb2-c1b6-4c5b) has been moved out of this epic.\n\nThe task moves the T201 per-file glob in `pyproject.toml` from `_engine/rebar_reconciler/*` to `reconciler/*` and drops the inline `# noqa: T201` markers. It depends on the dependency advisories tracked by f7dc-132b-057a-476c (unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis): any `pyproject.toml` edit trips the pip-audit dependency-map lane until those clear.\n\nWhile it was a child here, its `depends_on` f7dc was escalated to this epic. That made the epic unclaimable, and by the parent-first cascade it blocked every story.\n\nCoordinator decision, option 1:\n- Removed the escalated `friended-brainsick-degus → f7dc-132b-057a-476c depends_on` edge.\n- Detached likable-waterworn-willet to root level with `--parent=null`.\n- Re-linked it `depends_on` f7dc-132b-057a-476c directly, plus `discovered_from` this epic for provenance.\n\nThis epic's stated scope is unchanged, since its description never named the T201 cleanup. The epic no longer inherits the advisory gate."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792543553594596619,"uuid":"d2ad9596-61f8-46de-9fed-527a18e5dbb9"}